.TH STARTUP-TIME-CHECK 8 "November 2026" "startup-time-checker 1.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
startup-time-check \- wait during boot until the startup-time lock has passed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B startup-time-check
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run by
.I startup-time-checker.service
before
.IR sysinit.target .
Reads the lock time written by
.BR startup-time (1)
and waits, printing the time left on the console every 10 seconds, until it has
passed. A missing or unparsable state file never blocks booting.
.SH ESCAPE
Boot with
.B systemd.mask=startup-time-checker.service
on the kernel command line, then run
.BR "sudo startup-time clear" .
.SH FILES
.I /var/lib/startup-time.state
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR startup-time (1)
